# Ticket standard

- Use `docs/tickets/TEMPLATE.md`; one ticket owns one independently reviewable concern.
- Use IDs `TTW-XXX` and imperative outcome titles.
- Declare risk, status, dependencies, and reverse dependencies.
- Background states the observed problem with file/line or reproduction evidence; it does not prescribe the solution.
- Proposal names interfaces and deliberate trade-offs.
- State behavioural and data invariants for refactors and high-risk work.
- Keep implementation steps ordered and update them when implementation diverges.
- Acceptance criteria must be independently observable commands, tests, or behaviours.
- Name explicit out-of-scope work and its owning ticket.
- Append design reviews, implementation review iterations, evidence, deviations, and completion summary to the same ticket file.
- Keep `docs/tickets/README.md` in sync when present; do not create separate log files.
